Architecture Type

React (Vite) + Convex (Serverless Backend + Database)

Frontend (React + Vite)
        |
Convex Client (convex/react)
        |
Convex Backend (Functions + Database)
        |
Convex Cloud Database
        |
Stripe / Razorpay
        |
Cloud Deployment (Vercel)
🧠 Architecture Layers
1️⃣ Frontend

React + Vite

Tailwind CSS

Convex React client

Clerk/Auth0 (optional for auth)

2️⃣ Backend (Convex)

Convex Queries (read operations)

Convex Mutations (write operations)

Convex Actions (external API calls like payments)

Built-in database

3️⃣ Database

Convex document database

Schema defined in schema.ts

Automatic indexing

🗄 2. DATABASE DESIGN (Convex Schema)

Convex uses document-based schema.

📁 convex/schema.ts
Users
users: defineTable({
  name: v.string(),
  email: v.string(),
  role: v.union(v.literal("admin"), v.literal("user")),
  isActive: v.boolean(),
})
.index("by_email", ["email"])

Activities
activities: defineTable({
  title: v.string(),
  description: v.string(),
  images: v.array(v.string()),
  location: v.string(),
  difficulty: v.string(),
  duration: v.string(),
  price: v.number(),
  availableDates: v.array(v.string()),
  slotsAvailable: v.number(),
  createdBy: v.id("users"),
})
.index("by_location", ["location"])

Cart
carts: defineTable({
  userId: v.id("users"),
  activityIds: v.array(v.id("activities")),
  totalAmount: v.number(),
})
.index("by_user", ["userId"])

Bookings
bookings: defineTable({
  userId: v.id("users"),
  activityIds: v.array(v.id("activities")),
  amount: v.number(),
  paymentStatus: v.string(),
  bookingStatus: v.string(),
  paymentId: v.optional(v.string()),
})
.index("by_user", ["userId"])

Blogs
blogs: defineTable({
  title: v.string(),
  content: v.string(),
  slug: v.string(),
  authorId: v.id("users"),
})
.index("by_slug", ["slug"])